  message: "Closed retroactively during Phase 0 execution (2026-05-13). Fix landed in commit be0ddcb8eb 2026-05-12 ('feat(analyzers): WI-tihup + WI-mafik PR2 — 7-language dst_ref adoption + consumer migration'). That commit's message explicitly listed this item among 'Seven WI-mafik children close done with rationale acceptance criterion met — xfail removed in this PR' but the tracker mutation was missed. Verified today: polyglot_call_site_coverage test passes for this language (8/8); direct probe confirms expected (module, callable) substrings appear in calls-edge dsts. The work is done; only the tracker state was stale. Probe evidence: cpp:cstdio,cstring,cstdlib:0-0:printf:unresolved — comma-joined-include hint pattern (per commit message); polyglot fixture substring match is satisfied."  # 499b
